WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.203
Welcome to BidStream, your workspace for turning public tender
information

00:00:04.203 --> 00:00:08.406
into a clear next action. Over the next ten minutes,

00:00:08.406 --> 00:00:12.609
we will explore the complete demo, from choosing a company

00:00:12.609 --> 00:00:16.812
and discovering opportunities, to preparing an expression of
interest and

00:00:16.812 --> 00:00:21.014
reviewing a tender. Follow the highlighted cursor as we go.

00:00:21.014 --> 00:00:25.217
The aim is simple: spend less time organising information, and

00:00:25.217 --> 00:00:29.000
more time deciding which opportunities deserve your team's
attention.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.028
Start with the working company selector. Sweroad represents the
transport

00:00:34.028 --> 00:00:38.056
consultancy vertical, while ERP Software Technologies represents
software and IT

00:00:38.056 --> 00:00:42.083
services. Changing the company changes the matching context and
the

00:00:42.083 --> 00:00:46.111
shortlist you are working with. Check this selector before saving

00:00:46.111 --> 00:00:50.139
an opportunity. You can explore both verticals in the same

00:00:50.139 --> 00:00:54.167
workspace, while keeping each company's pursuits separate. These
are demonstration

00:00:54.167 --> 00:00:58.194
profiles, so verify their details before using them for a

00:00:58.194 --> 00:00:59.000
real submission.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:03.973
Open Companies to review the information behind your matches.
Describe

00:01:03.973 --> 00:01:07.945
what the business actually delivers, the countries it serves, and

00:01:07.945 --> 00:01:11.918
the capabilities that make it relevant. Add the company website

00:01:11.918 --> 00:01:15.890
and contact email, then complete the supporting company
information. Specific

00:01:15.890 --> 00:01:19.863
descriptions work better than broad claims. For example, an ERP

00:01:19.863 --> 00:01:23.836
implementation capability is more useful than simply saying
technology. Save

00:01:23.836 --> 00:01:27.808
your changes, then return to discovery to review opportunities
against

00:01:27.808 --> 00:01:29.000
that updated context.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:33.973
Company information also supports document preparation. Record
legal registrations, reference

00:01:33.973 --> 00:01:37.945
projects and useful company notes, using facts your team can

00:01:37.945 --> 00:01:41.918
substantiate. A contact email identifies the company, but
entering it

00:01:41.918 --> 00:01:45.890
does not connect a mailbox. In this demo, profiles and

00:01:45.890 --> 00:01:49.863
pursuit records stay in this browser. Use the workspace backup

00:01:49.863 --> 00:01:53.836
export to keep a copy. Profile import adds company profiles;

00:01:53.836 --> 00:01:57.808
it is not a complete restore of every exported pursuit

00:01:57.808 --> 00:01:59.000
and team record.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:03.816
Now open Discover. The demo brings together bounded public feeds

00:02:03.816 --> 00:02:07.632
from the World Bank and TED, and ranks notices against

00:02:07.632 --> 00:02:11.447
your selected company. Use the search field to focus on

00:02:11.447 --> 00:02:15.263
a service, technology or project theme. Market and source filters

00:02:15.263 --> 00:02:19.079
help narrow the list further. A minimum fit filter can

00:02:19.079 --> 00:02:22.895
reduce noise. Refresh sources when you need an updated view,

00:02:22.895 --> 00:02:26.711
remembering that this is a limited discovery feed, rather than

00:02:26.711 --> 00:02:29.000
every procurement portal on the internet.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:33.766
Open an opportunity to inspect the scope and the reasons

00:02:33.766 --> 00:02:37.532
behind its score. Matching combines capability keywords,
geography and scope

00:02:37.532 --> 00:02:41.299
signals. It is a transparent relevance heuristic, not an
artificial

00:02:41.299 --> 00:02:45.065
intelligence assessment of eligibility or a prediction that you
will

00:02:45.065 --> 00:02:48.831
win. Read the buyer's original notice before committing time.
Check

00:02:48.831 --> 00:02:52.597
mandatory qualifications, submission method, document
availability and the actual closing

00:02:52.597 --> 00:02:56.364
time. A high fit score is a reason to investigate,

00:02:56.364 --> 00:02:59.000
not a reason to skip due diligence.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:03.867
Use deadline information and sorting to choose what to inspect

00:03:03.867 --> 00:03:07.733
next. Best fit helps with relevance; closing soon helps with

00:03:07.733 --> 00:03:11.600
urgency; newest helps with fresh discovery. Treat missing dates
as

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:15.467
a task to verify, and check whether a closed notice

00:03:15.467 --> 00:03:19.333
has a published extension. If you find a suitable notice

00:03:19.333 --> 00:03:23.200
outside the connected feeds, add it manually with its source

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:27.067
link and scope. Exporting the visible results to CSV supports

00:03:27.067 --> 00:03:29.000
an offline review with colleagues.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:33.867
When an opportunity deserves attention, click Shortlist. The
saved notice

00:03:33.867 --> 00:03:37.733
moves into a separate section for the active company, so

00:03:37.733 --> 00:03:41.600
you can stop scanning and start preparing. Open Shortlist to

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:45.467
review your selected pursuits and work through them individually.
If

00:03:45.467 --> 00:03:49.333
you save the wrong item, removal includes an undo action.

00:03:49.333 --> 00:03:53.200
For this walkthrough, we use an explicitly labelled training
opportunity.

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:57.067
Its details illustrate the workflow and do not represent an

00:03:57.067 --> 00:03:59.000
invitation from a real buyer.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:03.766
Return to Dashboard for a practical view of the pipeline.

00:04:03.766 --> 00:04:07.532
The summary counts shortlisted opportunities, manually recorded
sent expressions of

00:04:07.532 --> 00:04:11.299
interest, recorded responses and items needing attention. Below,
the next

00:04:11.299 --> 00:04:15.065
action list uses deadline and stage information to guide your

00:04:15.065 --> 00:04:18.831
work. Filter for drafting or awaiting response when you need

00:04:18.831 --> 00:04:22.597
focus. These counts reflect your saved records, not a connected

00:04:22.597 --> 00:04:26.364
email inbox. Direct tender suggestions also appear here, so a

00:04:26.364 --> 00:04:29.000
suitable tender can enter your pipeline immediately.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:33.867
Open a pursuit to enter its workspace. The overview brings

00:04:33.867 --> 00:04:37.733
the opportunity, stage, notes and next steps together. Choose the

00:04:37.733 --> 00:04:41.600
route that matches the buyer's process: an expression of interest

00:04:41.600 --> 00:04:45.467
first, or a direct tender. Software procurement may start
directly

00:04:45.467 --> 00:04:49.333
with a tender, so there is no need to force

00:04:49.333 --> 00:04:53.200
an EOI stage. Verify the procedure and deadline on the

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:57.067
original notice. Keep decision notes here so the reason for

00:04:57.067 --> 00:04:59.000
pursuing the work remains visible.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:03.919
Next, open Requirements. Add the buyer's evaluation criteria,
either individually

00:05:03.919 --> 00:05:07.838
or as a list, then refine each item. Record its

00:05:07.838 --> 00:05:11.757
weight, whether it is mandatory, and the evidence you can

00:05:11.757 --> 00:05:15.676
provide. Use the actual tender wording where possible. This
creates

00:05:15.676 --> 00:05:19.595
a practical checklist for drafting and review. Weight totals
matter:

00:05:19.595 --> 00:05:23.514
the evaluation expects one hundred percent. A mandatory criterion
deserves

00:05:23.514 --> 00:05:27.432
special attention, because a strong average score cannot
compensate for

00:05:27.432 --> 00:05:29.000
failing a required qualification.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:33.816
The Team area helps you maintain an internal directory of

00:05:33.816 --> 00:05:37.632
experts, with roles, skills, evidence and availability. Within a
pursuit,

00:05:37.632 --> 00:05:41.447
select the people relevant to that assignment. Suggestions use
skill

00:05:41.447 --> 00:05:45.263
keywords from the scope, so review them carefully and confirm

00:05:45.263 --> 00:05:49.079
that the proposed team is genuinely suitable and available.
External

00:05:49.079 --> 00:05:52.895
recruitment and consultancy networks are not connected in this
demo.

00:05:52.895 --> 00:05:56.711
Naukri is a possible future integration, not a live source

00:05:56.711 --> 00:05:59.000
of candidate profiles in this release.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:03.919
Open Draft and create the document for your chosen route.

00:06:03.919 --> 00:06:07.838
BidStream assembles an editable starting point from company
information, the

00:06:07.838 --> 00:06:11.757
opportunity scope, requirements evidence and selected staff. This
is template

00:06:11.757 --> 00:06:15.676
based generation, not a complete expert written proposal. Read
every

00:06:15.676 --> 00:06:19.595
section and replace missing information with verified content.
The benefit

00:06:19.595 --> 00:06:23.514
is a structured place to begin, with relevant inputs brought

00:06:23.514 --> 00:06:27.432
together, so your team can concentrate on the response rather

00:06:27.432 --> 00:06:29.000
than an empty page.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:33.816
Use the draft health checks to find placeholders, missing
evidence

00:06:33.816 --> 00:06:37.632
and missing company references. Edit the document directly and
make

00:06:37.632 --> 00:06:41.447
the response specific to the buyer's requirements. Download a
text

00:06:41.447 --> 00:06:45.263
copy for further formatting or review. If you rebuild after

00:06:45.263 --> 00:06:49.079
changing your inputs, the workflow provides a download of the

00:06:49.079 --> 00:06:52.895
previous draft to help preserve your work. Always confirm the

00:06:52.895 --> 00:06:56.711
final submission format, page limits and required attachments in
the

00:06:56.711 --> 00:06:59.000
original procurement documents before sending anything.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:03.816
After submitting through the buyer's required channel, open
Submission and

00:07:03.816 --> 00:07:07.632
response. Record the document type, submission date and receipt
or

00:07:07.632 --> 00:07:11.447
reference. Add the buyer contact and an expected response date

00:07:11.447 --> 00:07:15.263
when you have a reasonable basis for one. This creates

00:07:15.263 --> 00:07:19.079
a follow-up record and updates the dashboard. The distinction
matters:

00:07:19.079 --> 00:07:22.895
saving a sent record does not send a message or

00:07:22.895 --> 00:07:26.711
upload a tender. The actual submission still takes place outside

00:07:26.711 --> 00:07:29.000
this demo through the authorised channel.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:33.671
When a buyer responds, record the date, response type and

00:07:33.671 --> 00:07:37.342
useful details in the same workspace. You can distinguish an

00:07:37.342 --> 00:07:41.013
acknowledgement, a clarification, a positive response or a
negative outcome.

00:07:41.013 --> 00:07:44.684
A positive EOI response can lead into tender preparation, with

00:07:44.684 --> 00:07:48.354
a new invitation deadline to verify and record. The activity

00:07:48.354 --> 00:07:52.025
history preserves your manual updates. Automatic mailbox checking
and daily

00:07:52.025 --> 00:07:55.696
response collection are not connected yet, so your team must

00:07:55.696 --> 00:07:59.000
enter these replies for the dashboard to reflect them.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:03.766
Before finalising a tender, open Evaluate. Review each criterion
against

00:08:03.766 --> 00:08:07.532
its supporting evidence and enter a reviewer score from zero

00:08:07.532 --> 00:08:11.299
to five. The weighted result helps structure an internal review,

00:08:11.299 --> 00:08:15.065
while missing evidence and mandatory gaps remain visible. It is

00:08:15.065 --> 00:08:18.831
not an independent semantic assessment of your proposal. Treat it

00:08:18.831 --> 00:08:22.597
as a disciplined checklist: strengthen weak evidence, resolve
mandatory gaps,

00:08:22.597 --> 00:08:26.364
and have a qualified colleague challenge the ratings before
relying

00:08:26.364 --> 00:08:29.000
on the result for a submission decision.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:33.718
Historical competition can inform a discussion, but only when the

00:08:33.718 --> 00:08:37.436
underlying evidence is sound. The demo lets you record a

00:08:37.436 --> 00:08:41.154
source link, a sample count and notes about previous competition.

00:08:41.154 --> 00:08:44.872
It does not contain a historical tender dataset or calculate

00:08:44.872 --> 00:08:48.590
a reliable probability of winning. Keep facts separate from
assumptions,

00:08:48.590 --> 00:08:52.308
and note when information is incomplete. The useful outcome is

00:08:52.308 --> 00:08:56.026
a better documented decision about whether to proceed, seek a

00:08:56.026 --> 00:08:59.000
partner, improve the proposal or decline the opportunity.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:03.973
Open Sources and Connections to understand coverage. World Bank
and

00:09:03.973 --> 00:09:07.945
TED discovery are available; other listed portals may require
manual

00:09:07.945 --> 00:09:11.918
access or future integration. Mailbox authentication, scheduled
response checks, recruitment

00:09:11.918 --> 00:09:15.890
APIs and automatic EOI sending are not operational in this

00:09:15.890 --> 00:09:19.863
release. The interface makes those boundaries visible. The UX
guide

00:09:19.863 --> 00:09:23.836
explains the design approach, and Product review gives a candid

00:09:23.836 --> 00:09:27.808
self-assessment. Neither replaces user testing, procurement
expertise or validation of

00:09:27.808 --> 00:09:29.000
a production integration.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:33.766
You now have the complete BidStream workflow. Choose the right

00:09:33.766 --> 00:09:37.532
company, refine its evidence, discover relevant notices and
shortlist the

00:09:37.532 --> 00:09:41.299
opportunities worth pursuing. Let the dashboard guide your next
action,

00:09:41.299 --> 00:09:45.065
prepare the appropriate document, review it against the buyer's
criteria,

00:09:45.065 --> 00:09:48.831
and track submissions and replies. Export your workspace backup
regularly,

00:09:48.831 --> 00:09:52.597
because this demo stores work on your device. Start with

00:09:52.597 --> 00:09:56.364
one opportunity, keep the source documents close, and turn a

00:09:56.364 --> 00:09:59.000
promising match into a well prepared response.
